  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "On a Shang clan city battle stage, Li Hao faces a charging opponent, activates position swap Gu, and vanishes to his Mountain Back Toad’s spot while the toad takes his former place. The toad then jumps and ends the fight. Spectators say the Gu can swap the toad’s location and can also swap with an opponent, covering the toad’s low movement speed.",
        "chapters": [
          289
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_shang_clan_city",
          "char_li_hao",
          "gu_mountain_back_toad"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan reasons that rainbow light Gu and position swap Gu need a Gu Master free of strength modifications, because strength Dao marks interfere with the law of space and can make the Gu fail.",
        "chapters": [
          292
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "strength-path-conflict",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_rainbow_light_gu",
          "sys_gu_master",
          "sys_dao_marks"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "After the battle with Li Hao, Fang Yuan gains three Gu worms but not the mountain back toad or position swap Gu. He beat the toad to death, and position swap Gu, as Li Hao’s vital Gu, perishes with Li Hao.",
        "chapters": [
          293
        ],
